  "content": {
    "id": "p14-p1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Show that $f(x)=\\dfrac{2^{2x}+1}{2^x}$ is an even function.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$f(-x)=2^{-x}+2^x=f(x)$, so $f$ is even.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=2^x+2^{-x}\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{2^{-2x}+1}{2^{-x}}\\\\f(-x)&=2^{-x}+2^x\\\\f(-x)&=f(x).\\end{align*}$$\nThe domain is $\\mathbb R$, and $f(-x)=f(x)$ for every real $x$. Hence $f$ is even.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 30
  },
